# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  JUNE FENN — Stargazer, seventeen
#  Sardonic, impatient, astronomy nerd, poetic in spite of herself.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

=== june.talk
[if $lantern_night] -> june.lantern
[if not $met_june] -> june.first
[if delivered("far_shore") == "june" and not $june_after_far] -> june.after_far
[if delivered("lamp_room") == "june" and not $june_after_lamp] -> june.after_lamp
[if $june_mum and not $june_after_bird] -> june.after_bird
-> june.default

=== june.first
~ set met_june
n: *A girl in a yellow raincoat sits at the very end of the pier, one eye screwed shut against a brass telescope.*
june: If you're here to tell me it's cold, I know. If you're here to tell me it's late, it's always late. If you're here to tell me to come home, tell Mum I'm *thinking*.
wren: I'm just the new night clerk.
june[surprised]: ...Oh. Huh. Odile actually hired someone. I had five shillings on "never".
june: I'm June. That's Vega, that's Deneb, and that's a gull. You can tell the gull because it's eating a chip.
* What are you looking for? -> june.first.looking
* Isn't it always dusk here? -> june.first.dusk

=== june.first.looking
june[thinking]: The edge. Where the sky goes from violet to that thin gold line. If you look long enough, you can almost see it move.
june[sad]: It doesn't, though. It hasn't moved since I was born. Everyone says the sun's just *there*, under the sea, like a coin under a sofa.
june: I've never seen it come up. Not once. Seventeen years.
-> june.first.end

=== june.first.dusk
june: Always. The sun went down the night of the Long Storm and just... stopped. Like it forgot its lines.
june[sad]: I was six months old. I've never seen it rise. Not once.
-> june.first.end

=== june.first.end
~ clue c4_june_sunrise
june[thinking]: There are places where it comes up every single morning. Like it's nothing. Like it's *cheap*.
june: I'm going to see one. Soon.
n: *She pats her coat pocket — then catches herself, and pretends she was brushing off a crumb.*

=== june.default
[if $june_path == "stay"] june[happy]: Grandpa let me trim the wick last night. He stood behind me the entire time breathing like a walrus. It was the best night of my life.
[if $june_path == "leave"] june: I counted the stairs with Grandpa. One hundred and twelve. He told me the name of every single star from the top. Rosa's Crown is the little one. It's crooked. It's perfect.
[if $june_path == ""] june: Clear night. Well. Clear-ish. Same as every night, if you don't count the clouds, which I do, professionally.
* What can you see tonight? -> june.sky
* Tell me about your family. -> june.family
* See you around. -> END

=== june.sky
[if pick(3) == 0] june[happy]: Jupiter, low in the east, being smug. Four moons. Galileo saw those with a worse telescope than mine. I think about that a lot.
[if pick(3) == 1] june: The Pleiades. Seven sisters. You can only see six. Nobody agrees on what happened to the seventh. I think she left town.
[if pick(3) == 2] june[thinking]: A satellite, going over. Somebody somewhere launched that. Somebody *went* somewhere.

=== june.family
june: Mum runs the bakery. Grandpa runs the lighthouse. Dad... was on the Marguerite. I don't remember him.
june[thinking]: We're a family of people who stay up all night looking after things. Bread. Lamps. Me.
june[sad]: Sometimes I'd like to be the thing that goes somewhere, instead of the thing that's looked after.

=== june.after_far
~ set june_after_far
june[happy]: Grandpa's teaching me the lamp. Well — he's teaching me to *watch* him do the lamp. Baby steps. A hundred and twelve of them.
june: I'm still going, Wren. On the 6:10. But now when I go, I'll know what's up those stairs.
june[shy]: Thanks. For the letter. For... whoever I'm going to be.

=== june.after_lamp
~ set june_after_lamp
june: Whole heart. I keep saying it to myself. Whole heart, whole heart. It sounds like a heartbeat if you say it fast enough.
june[happy]: Grandpa cried when I told him. He'll deny it. He said it was "lamp smoke". The lamp wasn't lit.

=== june.after_bird
~ set june_after_bird
june[shy]: I helped Mum with the lantern loaves. Don't make a thing of it.
june[happy]: She's been humming all evening. Mum doesn't hum. It's deeply unsettling.

=== june.lantern
[if $finale] -> june.finale
[if $june_path == "leave"] june: Bag's packed. Grandpa gave me his old star chart. Mum gave me eleven loaves. I can't carry eleven loaves, Wren.
[if $june_path == ""] june[sad]: Lantern Night. Everyone's so... sad and nice. I hate it. I'm leaving on the 6:10 tomorrow. Don't tell anyone.
[if $june_path == ""] june: Not that anyone would notice.

=== june.finale
[if $june_path == "leave"] june[happy]: When the sun comes up — *if* it comes up — I'll be on the ferry going towards it. That's the plan. That's the whole plan.
[if $june_path == ""] june[thinking]: Look at all the lanterns. Dad's in there somewhere. Somewhere up there in all that.

# ─── Ask about clues ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

=== june.ask.c3_stargazer
june[happy]: Stargazer? That's... that's what Dad used to call me. Apparently. I was a baby, I don't remember. Grandpa told me.
june[thinking]: Who's calling me that? What have you got?
~ clue c3_june_scope

=== june.ask.c3_june_scope
june: It was Grandpa's. Before that, his grandmother's. She used it to spot wrecks. I use it to spot the edge of everything.

=== june.ask.c3_ferry
june[surprised]: Who told you about the ferry? Was it Bram? It was Bram. Bram couldn't keep a secret in a locked safe at the bottom of the sea.
june[sad]: ...Yes. I've got a ticket. One way. The morning after Lantern Night. Don't tell Mum.
~ clue c3_manifest

=== june.ask.c3_manifest
-> june.ask.c3_ferry

=== june.ask.c7_ticket
-> june.ask.c3_ferry

=== june.ask.c3_grandpa
june: Grandpa? Tobias Fenn, lighthouse keeper, world champion at saying nothing. He's up on the cliff. He lights the lamp by hand every night, like it'll bite him if he doesn't.
~ clue c3_granddaughter

=== june.ask.c3_granddaughter
june: Yep. Granddaughter. Only one. He says I'm "a lot". He's not wrong.

=== june.ask.c3_rosa_stars
june[surprised]: Stars he named for Grandma? He never — he's never told me that. He never tells me anything.
june[thinking]: There's a chart up in the lamp room. He won't let me up there. Says the stairs are "not a playground". I'm *seventeen*.

=== june.ask.c3_star_chart
june[surprised]: Rosa's Crown? He named them? Three little stars in the west — I've *looked* at those. I've looked at them a hundred times. I never knew they were hers.

=== june.ask.c3_postmark
june[thinking]: Twenty forty-six? That's... that's not funny. Where did you get this?
june: Southern Ocean. That's where the big research ships go. That's where I'd go. If I...
june[shy]: Never mind.

=== june.ask.c3_comet
june[happy]: A grumpy comet? Ha. If I ever found a comet, I'd want it grumpy. A comet with *opinions*.

=== june.ask.c34_same_hand
june[thinking]: Same handwriting, same date, two different lives? That's not a letter. That's a fork in the road that someone put a stamp on.

=== june.ask.c4_keeper
june[angry]: The *keeper*? Of the lighthouse? Me? No. No way. I'd rather eat my telescope.
june[sad]: ...Would I?

=== june.ask.c4_stairs
june: A hundred and twelve steps. It says so over the door. I counted them once when I was eight, and Grandpa caught me on step sixty. Never been higher.

=== june.ask.c4_112
-> june.ask.c4_stairs

=== june.ask.c4_sunrise
june[sad]: Never seen a sunrise. Yeah. That's me. That's my whole personality.
~ clue c4_june_sunrise

=== june.ask.c4_june_sunrise
june: Seventeen years of the same orange. It's like living inside a sentence that never gets to the full stop.

=== june.ask.c4_birthday
june[surprised]: The fourteenth of March is my birthday. How do you — oh. *Oh.* Both of them? On my birthday?
june[thinking]: Thirty-seven. I'll be thirty-seven. That's so *old*.

=== june.ask.c4_logpaper
june: Hushwater Light logbook paper. Grandpa orders it from a printer in Port Ardent. Says the cheap stuff "doesn't take ink honest".

=== june.ask.c7_bird
june[angry]: "Little bird"? Ugh. That's Mum. She calls me that. I hate it.
june[shy]: Don't tell her I said I hate it.
~ clue c7_june_bird

=== june.ask.c7_father
-> june.ask.c6_marguerite

=== june.ask.c7_uncle
june: My uncle? Theo. I don't remember him. Mum doesn't talk about him. Which means she talks about him constantly, just without saying his name.
~ clue c1_theo

=== june.ask.c6_marguerite
june[sad]: Dad was on the Marguerite. I've got one photo. He's holding me up like a fish he's caught. That's all I've got of him. A photo, and his name on a stone.
~ clue c6_june_daniel

=== june.ask.c6_memorial
-> june.ask.c6_marguerite

=== june.ask.c6_daniel
-> june.ask.c6_marguerite

=== june.ask.c6_dark
june[sad]: Grandpa never talks about the night the lamp went out. Not once. That's how I know it's the only thing he thinks about.

=== june.ask.c6_felix_shift
june[surprised]: Felix was meant to be on the boat? Instead of Dad?
june[sad]: ...Huh. That's why he can't look at me. I always thought he just didn't like teenagers.

=== june.ask.c1_theo
june: Uncle Theo? I don't remember him. Mum doesn't talk about him. Which means she talks about him constantly, just without saying his name.

=== june.ask.c3_felix_scope
june[happy]: Felix's telescope? It's older than Felix. He uses it to set clocks, which is like using a violin to hammer nails.

=== june.ask.c2_pier
june: The end of the pier? You're standing on it. Best seat in Hushwater. Everyone ends up here eventually.

=== june.ask.c5_wheel
june[happy]: The man at the wheel is Bram. He lets me steer sometimes, when the sea's flat. Then he sings. Then I give the wheel back.

=== june.ask.default
[if pick(3) == 0] june: No idea. Ask me about stars. Ask me about anything that's more than four light-years away.
[if pick(3) == 1] june[thinking]: Hm. Nope. That's a ground-level problem. I'm more of an up person.
[if pick(3) == 2] june: Do I look like I know things? Don't answer that.
